  "Caption": "Finance called: at month-end, the gateway total and our invoice total differed by 147 units.\n\nSmall amount, but in accounting \u0022almost right\u0022 means \u0022wrong\u0022.\n\nThree mistakes caused it:\n1. double for money. 0.1 \u002B 0.2 is 0.30000000000000004, and thousands of lines accumulate the error.\n2. Rounding in different places with different rules. Math.Round defaults to banker\u0027s rounding (2.5 becomes 2), accounting usually wants AwayFromZero.\n3. Splitting 100 between 3 people without deciding who gets the remainder: 33.33 x 3 = 99.99.\n\nThe fix: decimal (or minor units as long), one explicit rounding policy, remainder allocation, and a Money value object that carries the currency.\n\nIn a financial system, one wrong cent is a bug that has not been discovered yet.\n\nWhat type do you use for money?\n\n#CSharp #Fintech #DDD #BugStories",
